<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Qara Qoyunlu</h1><p class="st-meta">1374 CE – 1468 CE (approx.) · capital Tabriz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Turkmen confederation, the 'Black Sheep', that ruled Azerbaijan, Iraq and much of Iran in the 15th century until defeated by the rival White Sheep.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Qara Qoyunlu were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oghuz-turks">Oghuz</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> tribes of the region around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-van">Lake Van</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a>. Their leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayram-khwaja">Bayram Khwaja</a> emerged in the 1370s as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jalayirids">Jalayirids</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-yusuf">Qara Yusuf</a> fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>, fled to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a>, returned after Timur's death and in 1410 defeated and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-jalayir">Ahmad Jalayir</a>, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The confederation was ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-yusuf">Qara Yusuf</a> family through tribal leaders and Persian officials, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> as capital. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-iskander">Iskandar</a> fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurid</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-rukh">Shah Rukh</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jahan-shah-qara-qoyunlu">Jahan Shah</a> (1438 to 1467) expanded the state to its greatest extent, briefly taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herat">Herat</a> in 1458, and wrote poetry in Turkic and Persian; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blue-mosque-of-tabriz">Blue Mosque of Tabriz</a> was built in his reign. The dynasty has been associated with Shia sympathies, though this is debated.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1467 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzun-hasan">Uzun Hasan</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a> defeated and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jahan-shah-qara-qoyunlu">Jahan Shah</a>. His son Hasan Ali was defeated in 1468, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a> absorbed the state.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/qara-qoyunlu.jpg" alt="Qara Qoyunlu" width="320" height="217"><figcaption>Image: Demis Map Server · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Timurid_and_Qara_Qoyunlu_domains,_1458.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1374 CE – 1468 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tabriz</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Qara Yusuf, Iskandar, Jahan Shah</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Azerbaijani Turkic, Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a>, <a href="/countries/iraq">Iraq</a>, <a href="/countries/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>, <a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>, <a href="/countries/armenia">Armenia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kara Koyunlu, Black Sheep Turkomans, Qara Qoyunlu Confederation</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1421&amp;focus=qara-qoyunlu" aria-label="Qara Qoyunlu on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5833 809 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Qara Qoyunlu lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6153 1065L6019 1090M6153 1065L5974 1011M6153 1065L6003 1071M6153 1065L6134 1224M6153 1065L6582 1190M6153 1065L6241 1288"/><pat